index ca88eec..d8126ce 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -161,6 +161,17 @@ Minecraft can't (a scripted scene, a web, a lever, a menu) or just to play Skyri
   with a Minecraft screen (inventory, chat) open.
 - It's keyboard-only for now, like the rest of SkyCraft's input.
 
+### Mob stand-ins (lock-on, health bars, sound)
+
+Each Minecraft mob near you has an invisible Skyrim actor (its stand-in) for lock-on mods and Skyrim's spells to work on.
+
+- The stand-in faces the way the mob faces and is placed so that its **head** is at the mob's eyes. It follows the mob every frame
+  (carried on by the mob's velocity between Minecraft's ten reports a second), so the lock-on marker rides the mob's head smoothly.
+- Its **health is the mob's, 1:1**: same maximum, same current value, updated with every report. Damage Skyrim does to it is passed on to
+  the mob; the stand-in is essential, so a big hit can't leave a dead skeever lying where the mob stands.
+- It is made from a rabbit by default (no growls or hisses). `sStandInBase` in `SkyCraft.ini` `[Mobs]` picks another creature, or a
+  silent actor from a mod (`Plugin.esp:0xFORMID`). `Skeever` restores the old behaviour.
+
 ## Known limitations
 
 - If something goes wrong, `Documents\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE\SkyCraft.log` says what.
